<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n59467" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κούρ-ιμος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Agatho
			3
		</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
			11.3
		</span></i>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κουρά</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of, for cutting hair</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σίδαρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					966
				</span></i>
			 (nisi cum <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάρα</span> jungendum).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>shorn off</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαίτη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					180
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θρίξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					521
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Agatho
			</span></i> l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>shorn</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρᾶτα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					279
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. σχῆμα ἀναλαμβάνειν</span>
			<i>tonsure</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Pel.</u>
				34
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> as
				Subst., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ κούριμος</span>
			<i>Tragic mask</i> for mourners, <i>with the hair cut close,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				7.37
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Diosc.
			</span></i>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				4.140
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
